{'strand': 'social', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'g9-courtesy-aware', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S3.12.1; SHAPE.S3.12.2', 'assumes': 'g8-leading', 'hands_on': 'g10-safe-habits', 'model_in': 'team-talk; safe-space', 'model_out': 'team-talk; safe-space', 'words': 'courtesy; respect; teamwork; aware; empathy; etiquette', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Be aware of how others feel and think during activity, and show courtesy, respect and teamwork. Assessed by conduct against stated behaviors during team tasks.'}
{'strand': 'social', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'g9-encourage-feedback', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S3.12.3; SHAPE.S3.12.4', 'assumes': 'g8-leading', 'hands_on': 'g10-challenges-leadership', 'model_in': 'team-talk; skill-analysis', 'model_out': 'team-talk; skill-analysis', 'words': 'encourage; feedback; coach; observe; specific; peer', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Encourage and support others, and offer feedback on others' performance without waiting for the teacher to ask, using a cue sheet. Assessed by conduct: gives specific feedback unprompted in a peer task."}
{'strand': 'fitness-and-choice', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'g9-choose-active', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S4.12.1; ~SHAPE.S4.12.2; ~SHAPE.S4.12.3; ~SHAPE.S4.12.4; ~SHAPE.S4.12.5', 'assumes': 'g8-goals-obstacles; g8-reflect', 'hands_on': 'g10-choose-active-apply', 'model_in': 'goal-cycle; calm-steps', 'model_out': 'goal-cycle; calm-steps', 'words': 'choice; interest; challenge level; health; social; expression', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Samples activities in many kinds (dance, yoga, aerobics, a sport, an outdoor activity) and records what each one gave: expression, company, health, fit with interests, challenge level. Works toward the choosing indicators owned in grade 10. Assessed by a knowledge task: a one-page activity log kept privately.'}
{'strand': 'motor', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-outdoor', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S1.12.3', 'assumes': 'g9-lifetime-sport-skills', 'hands_on': 'g11-chosen-activity-skills', 'model_in': 'skill-analysis', 'model_out': 'skill-analysis', 'words': 'trail; navigation; paddle; climb; ski; cycle', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Do the key moves of a range of outdoor activities the school can offer (hiking, orienteering, paddling, cycling, climbing, snow sports where local): the moves, gear and pace. Assessed by a skill task: key moves of one or two activities. Teacher note: weather, route, helmets and ratio set by the school; stay in groups.'}
{'strand': 'motor', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-stretch-technique', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S1.12.7', 'assumes': 'g9-aerobic-form; g9-strength-form', 'hands_on': 'g11-training-form', 'model_in': 'skill-analysis; fitt-plan', 'model_out': 'skill-analysis; fitt-plan', 'words': 'flexibility; static; dynamic; range; hold', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Use correct technique when stretching to build flexibility: dynamic stretches in warm-ups, static holds after training, held thirty seconds without bouncing. Assessed by a skill task: stretches for six large muscle groups with form. Teacher note: stretch warm muscles only; never to pain.'}
{'strand': 'motor', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-skill-fitness-training', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S1.12.8', 'assumes': 'g9-lifetime-sport-skills; g8-fitness-dance-apply; g7-skill-fitness-use', 'hands_on': 'g11-chosen-activity-skills; g11-training-form', 'model_in': 'skill-analysis; fitt-plan; fitness-parts', 'model_out': 'skill-analysis; fitt-plan; fitness-parts', 'words': 'agility; power; plyometric; reaction time; speed; coordination', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Use correct technique when training the skill-related fitness parts: agility drills, reaction drills, low plyometrics, balance and coordination work. Assessed by a skill task: a short session with form checked. Teacher note: soft surface; low heights only; volume small. Returns to g8-fitness-dance-apply and g7-skill-fitness-use after a skip: the grade 9 sport rows use these drills.'}
{'strand': 'motor', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-water', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S1.12.9; SHAPE.S2.12.17', 'assumes': 'g8-water', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'safe-space', 'model_out': 'safe-space', 'words': 'swim; survival; rescue; hypothermia; current; lifeguard', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Show water safety and simple swimming where a pool is available: survival float, a stroke, reach and throw rescues, cold-water and current risks, and what to do in an emergency. The handoff skips grade 9 because water units run where a pool exists. Assessed by a knowledge task and a dry-land skill task for every school: a reach rescue, a throw rescue to a target and fastening a life jacket; in-water tasks only where a pool exists. Teacher note: No child is made to enter water. Any in-water task belongs to the school's own aquatics program, with a qualified lifeguard on site and the school's swim policy."}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-outdoor-tactics', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S2.12.3', 'assumes': 'g9-lifetime-tactics', 'hands_on': 'g11-tactics-in-chosen', 'model_in': 'tactics-question; skill-analysis', 'model_out': 'tactics-question; skill-analysis', 'words': 'route; pace; conditions; risk; navigation; plan', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Show understanding of tactics in outdoor activities: route choice, pacing, reading conditions, risk. Assessed by a knowledge task: plans a route or a trip and explains the choices.'}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-fitness-life', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S2.12.5; SHAPE.S2.12.11', 'assumes': 'g9-exercise-principles', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'fitt-plan; effort-scale', 'model_out': 'fitt-plan; effort-scale', 'words': 'quality of life; chronic disease; independence; early adulthood; lifestyle', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Examine how fitness and health shape quality of life after high school, and discuss the benefits of an active lifestyle in early adulthood. The health course units must name this row when they are written, so the same thing is not taught twice in a year. Assessed by a knowledge task: a short written or spoken case.'}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-mixed-plan', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S2.12.8', 'assumes': 'g9-exercise-principles; g9-effort-heart-rate', 'hands_on': 'g11-plan-for-self; g11-train-by-effort', 'model_in': 'fitt-plan; fitness-parts; effort-scale; goal-cycle', 'model_out': 'fitt-plan; fitness-parts; effort-scale; goal-cycle', 'words': 'program; endurance; strength; flexibility; schedule; log', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Make and follow a plan that mixes endurance, strength and flexibility training for several weeks: FITT per type, a weekly schedule, a log, and a change after a check. Assessed by a knowledge task: the plan, the log and one change. Teacher note: the plan and the log are private and never graded on results.'}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-rest', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S2.12.12', 'assumes': 'g9-exercise-principles; g7-rest', 'hands_on': 'g11-train-by-effort', 'model_in': 'fitt-plan; effort-scale', 'model_out': 'fitt-plan; effort-scale', 'words': 'recovery; sleep; rest day; overtraining; periodization', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Build rest into a regular activity schedule: rest days, sleep, signs of overtraining. Assessed by a knowledge task: adds rest to the plan and gives the reason. Returns to g7-rest after a skip: rest comes back inside the grade 9 principles row.'}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-games-culture', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S2.12.14; SHAPE.S3.12.5', 'assumes': 'g8-culture-matters', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'team-talk', 'model_out': 'team-talk', 'words': 'culture; history; society; tradition; identity; sport', 'cross_subject': 'social-studies:ss6-complex-societies (complex societies)', 'notes': 'Discuss how games, sports and dance have shaped societies and cultures over time, and examine how one activity is valued in different cultures. The handoff skips grade 9 because culture work returns with the social studies course here. The social studies course units must name this row when they are written, so the same thing is not taught twice in a year. Assessed by a knowledge task: a short case on one activity in two cultures. Cultural claims are sourced. Sacred or ceremonial activities: APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground.'}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-tech', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S2.12.15', 'assumes': 'g8-tech-judge', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'fitt-plan', 'model_out': 'fitt-plan', 'words': 'wearable; data; privacy; accuracy; app; evidence', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Examine and use technology that supports an active, healthy life: pick a tool, use it for two weeks, and judge what it showed. The handoff skips grade 9 because the technology judgment of grade 8 returns here with a tool in use. Assessed by a knowledge task. Teacher note: no tool is required; no data leaves the student.'}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-food', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S2.12.16', 'assumes': 'g7-eat-move-well', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'effort-scale', 'model_out': 'effort-scale', 'words': 'fuel; hydration; recovery; supplement; protein; performance', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Name foods that help or hurt performance, recovery and enjoyment of activity: water, timing of meals, and the limits of supplements and drinks. The handoff skips grades 8 and 9 because food and drink stay with the health course in those years. The health course units must name this row when they are written, so the same thing is not taught twice in a year. Assessed by a knowledge task. Teacher note: no body weight or calorie talk.'}
{'strand': 'social', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-safe-habits', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S3.12.6', 'assumes': 'g9-courtesy-aware; g8-outdoor-safety', 'hands_on': 'g11-safe-conduct', 'model_in': 'safe-space; team-talk', 'model_out': 'safe-space; team-talk', 'words': 'injury; sun; hydrate; equipment; space; protect', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Follow safe habits: prevent injury, give space, drink water, care for gear, follow rules, protect skin from sun. The handoff from grade 8 skips grade 9 because the safety checklist returns here in outdoor and gear-based settings. Assessed by conduct: follows a stated safety checklist during an outdoor or gear-based activity.'}
{'strand': 'social', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-challenges-leadership', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S3.12.7; SHAPE.S3.12.8', 'assumes': 'g9-encourage-feedback', 'hands_on': 'g11-lead-feedback', 'model_in': 'team-talk; tactics-question', 'model_out': 'team-talk; tactics-question', 'words': 'leader; challenge; teamwork; decision; evaluate; role', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Reason through challenges alone and in teams during activity, and judge how well leadership works in different activity settings (a team captain, a coach, a peer leader). Assessed by conduct and a knowledge task: leads a task and evaluates the leadership.'}
{'strand': 'fitness-and-choice', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'g10-choose-active-apply', 'standard': 'SHAPE.S4.12.1; SHAPE.S4.12.2; SHAPE.S4.12.3; SHAPE.S4.12.4; SHAPE.S4.12.5; SHAPE.S4.12.6; SHAPE.S4.12.7; SHAPE.S4.12.8; SHAPE.S4.12.9', 'assumes': 'g9-choose-active', 'hands_on': 'g11-express-company; g11-health-interests; g11-fitting-challenge; g12-manage-emotions', 'model_in': 'goal-cycle; calm-steps', 'model_out': 'goal-cycle; calm-steps', 'words': 'choice; calm; emotion; challenge; interest', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'The personal plan in short form, so every student meets the choice indicators in the two required years (Cory, 2026-11-20), with every part of each taught: picks and tries a different activity each term with a stated reason, among them one that lets the student express themselves (a dance, yoga or aerobics) and one with time with others; says how each fits health, interests and challenge level, and does well at a fitting level; sets movement goals tied to their own interests; looks at what affects staying active after high school (life choices, money, motivation, access); uses a chosen way to manage emotions during activity; and thinks over what PE has meant to them. Grades 11 and 12, the electives, deepen the plan. Assessed by a knowledge task (the log of choices and reasons, and a one-page plan to stay active after school with its goals and what may get in the way, ending in a short reflection) and by conduct (a chosen way to manage emotions used in a hard moment). Teacher note on emotions: APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground.'}
{'strand': 'motor', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'g11-chosen-activity-skills', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S1.12.1; ~SHAPE.S1.12.2; ~SHAPE.S1.12.3; ~SHAPE.S1.12.4; ~SHAPE.S2.12.4', 'assumes': 'g10-outdoor; g10-skill-fitness-training', 'hands_on': 'g12-lifelong-skills', 'model_in': 'skill-analysis; tactics-question', 'model_out': 'skill-analysis; tactics-question', 'words': 'chosen activity; technique; plan; refine; self-coach', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Applies the key skills of a lifetime sport, a casual game, an outdoor activity or a dance chosen by the student, with a technique check against a cue sheet. Grades 11 and 12 carry the motor indicators of the span. Assessed by a skill task in the chosen activity.'}
{'strand': 'motor', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'g11-training-form', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S1.12.5; ~SHAPE.S1.12.6; ~SHAPE.S1.12.7; ~SHAPE.S1.12.8; ~SHAPE.S2.12.13', 'assumes': 'g10-stretch-technique; g10-skill-fitness-training', 'hands_on': 'g12-fitness-technique', 'model_in': 'skill-analysis; fitt-plan; fitness-parts', 'model_out': 'skill-analysis; fitt-plan; fitness-parts', 'words': 'form; session; progression; warm-up; cool-down', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Applies correct form in aerobic, strength, flexibility and skill-related training inside the student's own program. Assessed by a skill task: a full session with form checked. Teacher note: no max lifts; trained spotter for loaded lifts."}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'g11-plan-for-self', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S2.12.6; ~SHAPE.S2.12.7; ~SHAPE.S2.12.8', 'assumes': 'g10-mixed-plan', 'hands_on': 'g12-own-program; g12-active-adult; g12-goals-interests', 'model_in': 'fitt-plan; fitness-parts; goal-cycle', 'model_out': 'fitt-plan; fitness-parts; goal-cycle', 'words': 'program; goal; principle; log; adjust; plan', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Applies exercise principles in the student's own program for a term, with a goal, a log and a mid-term change. Assessed by a knowledge task: the plan and a log summary. Logs and ratings are the student's own and private; they are never graded on results."}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'g11-train-by-effort', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S2.12.9; ~SHAPE.S2.12.10; ~SHAPE.S2.12.12', 'assumes': 'g10-rest; g10-mixed-plan', 'hands_on': 'g12-own-program', 'model_in': 'pulse-check; effort-scale; fitt-plan', 'model_out': 'pulse-check; effort-scale; fitt-plan', 'words': 'zone; effort; recovery; heart rate; rest', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Trains by effort and heart rate and builds rest in: zone choice by goal, an interval session, a recovery day. Assessed by a knowledge task: a session plan with effort ratings. Logs and ratings are the student's own and private; they are never graded on results."}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'g11-tactics-in-chosen', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S2.12.1; ~SHAPE.S2.12.2; ~SHAPE.S2.12.3', 'assumes': 'g10-outdoor-tactics', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'tactics-question; skill-analysis', 'model_out': 'tactics-question; skill-analysis', 'words': 'tactics; conditions; strategy; scouting; adapt; choose', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Applies tactics in the student's chosen sport, casual game or outdoor activity in a longer game or trip. Assessed by a knowledge task: explains tactics used in a recorded game or a trip log."}
{'strand': 'social', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'g11-lead-feedback', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S3.12.3; ~SHAPE.S3.12.4; ~SHAPE.S3.12.8', 'assumes': 'g10-challenges-leadership', 'hands_on': 'g12-lead', 'model_in': 'team-talk; skill-analysis', 'model_out': 'team-talk; skill-analysis', 'words': 'lead; mentor; coach; peer feedback; encourage', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Leads a small group in a skill or fitness session and gives unprompted, specific feedback. Assessed by conduct and a knowledge task: leads a session with a plan.'}
{'strand': 'social', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'g11-safe-conduct', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S3.12.2; ~SHAPE.S3.12.6', 'assumes': 'g10-safe-habits', 'hands_on': 'g12-community', 'model_in': 'safe-space; team-talk', 'model_out': 'safe-space; team-talk', 'words': 'safety; protect; respect; etiquette; space; gear', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Applies safe habits and courtesy as the usual way of acting in new activities, with students setting their own safety checklist. Assessed by conduct against the checklist.'}
{'strand': 'fitness-and-choice', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'g11-express-company', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S4.12.1; ~SHAPE.S4.12.2', 'assumes': 'g10-choose-active-apply', 'hands_on': 'g12-after-school; g12-reflect', 'model_in': 'goal-cycle; calm-steps', 'model_out': 'goal-cycle; calm-steps', 'words': 'express; yoga; aerobics; dance; company; club', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Choose and join activities, such as dance, yoga or aerobics, that let a student express themselves, and choose activities that offer time with others (a class, a club, a team). Assessed by a knowledge task and conduct: a chosen activity joined for a term with a reason. An elective year: deepens the grade 10 plan; the indicator is owned in grade 10.'}
{'strand': 'fitness-and-choice', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'g11-health-interests', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S4.12.3; ~SHAPE.S4.12.4', 'assumes': 'g10-choose-active-apply', 'hands_on': 'g12-goals-interests', 'model_in': 'goal-cycle; calm-steps', 'model_out': 'goal-cycle; calm-steps', 'words': 'health; interest; match; routine; habit; motivation', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Find and join an activity that improves health and one that matches interests, and explain the match. Assessed by a knowledge task: a short written reason for each choice. An elective year: deepens the grade 10 plan; the indicator is owned in grade 10.'}
{'strand': 'fitness-and-choice', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'g11-fitting-challenge', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S4.12.5', 'assumes': 'g10-choose-active-apply', 'hands_on': 'g12-after-school; g12-manage-emotions', 'model_in': 'goal-cycle; calm-steps', 'model_out': 'goal-cycle; calm-steps', 'words': 'challenge; success; level; skill; adapt; stretch', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Choose activity at a fitting challenge level and do well in it: pick a level from a range, adjust when too easy or hard. Assessed by a knowledge task and a skill task: a chosen level and a record of success. An elective year: deepens the grade 10 plan; the indicator is owned in grade 10.'}
{'strand': 'motor', 'grade': '12', 'skill_id': 'g12-lifelong-skills', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S1.12.1; ~SHAPE.S1.12.2; ~SHAPE.S1.12.3; ~SHAPE.S1.12.4', 'assumes': 'g11-chosen-activity-skills', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'skill-analysis; tactics-question', 'model_out': 'skill-analysis; tactics-question', 'words': 'lifelong; technique; refine; self-coach; independent', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Applies motor skills in activities the student will keep after school, with a self-written technique check. Assessed by a skill task in a chosen activity. New in grade 12: the student writes the cue sheet and coaches a partner.'}
{'strand': 'motor', 'grade': '12', 'skill_id': 'g12-fitness-technique', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S1.12.5; ~SHAPE.S1.12.6; ~SHAPE.S1.12.7; ~SHAPE.S1.12.8', 'assumes': 'g11-training-form', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'skill-analysis; fitt-plan; fitness-parts', 'model_out': 'skill-analysis; fitt-plan; fitness-parts', 'words': 'form; safety; program; session; coaching', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Applies correct form across training types in the student's own long-term program. Assessed by a skill task: a session coached by a partner. New in grade 12: a session the student designs and a partner coaches."}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '12', 'skill_id': 'g12-own-program', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S2.12.6; ~SHAPE.S2.12.7; ~SHAPE.S2.12.8; ~SHAPE.S2.12.10; ~SHAPE.S2.12.12', 'assumes': 'g11-plan-for-self; g11-train-by-effort', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'fitt-plan; fitness-parts; goal-cycle; pulse-check; effort-scale', 'model_out': 'fitt-plan; fitness-parts; goal-cycle; pulse-check; effort-scale', 'words': 'program; goal; progression; recovery; log; review', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Designs and follows a full program for a term with a goal, FITT per type, heart-rate or effort checks and rest, and reviews it. Assessed by a knowledge task: the program and a review. Teacher note: private records; no graded results.'}
{'strand': 'concepts', 'grade': '12', 'skill_id': 'g12-active-adult', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S2.12.5; ~SHAPE.S2.12.11; ~SHAPE.S2.12.15; ~SHAPE.S2.12.16', 'assumes': 'g11-plan-for-self', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'fitt-plan; effort-scale', 'model_out': 'fitt-plan; effort-scale', 'words': 'adult life; quality of life; technology; food; routine; sleep', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Plans an active week for early adulthood (work, study or a trade) with tools and food that support it. The health course units must name this row when they are written, so the same thing is not taught twice in a year. Assessed by a knowledge task: a one-week plan. Teacher note: no body weight or calorie talk.'}
{'strand': 'social', 'grade': '12', 'skill_id': 'g12-lead', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S3.12.3; ~SHAPE.S3.12.4; ~SHAPE.S3.12.7; ~SHAPE.S3.12.8', 'assumes': 'g11-lead-feedback', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'team-talk; tactics-question', 'model_out': 'team-talk; tactics-question', 'words': 'lead; organize; feedback; evaluate; event; team', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Leads or organizes a small activity event (a class game day, a skills clinic), gives feedback and evaluates the leadership. Assessed by conduct and a knowledge task: the event plan and an evaluation. New in grade 12: the student organizes an event, not a single session.'}
{'strand': 'social', 'grade': '12', 'skill_id': 'g12-community', 'standard': '~SHAPE.S3.12.1; ~SHAPE.S3.12.2; ~SHAPE.S3.12.5; ~SHAPE.S2.12.14', 'assumes': 'g11-safe-conduct', 'hands_on': '', 'model_in': 'safe-space; team-talk', 'model_out': 'safe-space; team-talk', 'words': 'community; culture; respect; inclusion; access; volunteer', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Applies courtesy and care in community-style activity and examines how a chosen activity is valued in other cultures. Assessed by conduct and a knowledge task: a short community activity case. Each cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it. Sacred or ceremonial activities: APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground.'}
