ble, and a spoken line on how it serves the purpose; DA:Cr2.1.Ib, a kept piece: the artist's statement on structure and elements, drafted, given written feedback after the critique and revised. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: blending established movement and styles (Level 2). Tools: source cards, the strengths test sheet, structure cards, the statement frame, Curio Class's own. Free path: sources from the room, a library book or a public domain poem. Short path: 16 days | After unit 2 because a dance is made from clear elements and rehearsed phrases; before unit 4 because a dance must exist to be reworked and recorded. The artist-statement model starts here. The mid-year check follows it | Candidate: a choreographer from Africa or Latin America whose source is a place, described and linked | Hazards and controls: as unit 2; group making on a marked floor with zones so groups do not collide. Hip hop's Philadelphia roots: the sensitivity agent reads the company's own published words first. Sources from a student's own life are invited, never required, with a public or invented source marked the same. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (moving unit). |
